opportunity_analysis.market_scoring:
Analyze this Polymarket opportunity and score it for trading potential:

MARKET: {market_title}
Description: {market_description}
Current Prices — YES: {yes_price_cents}¢  NO: {no_price_cents}¢
24h Volume: ${volume_24h}
Liquidity: ${liquidity}
End Date: {end_date}
PNL Potential Score: {pnl_potential} (higher = more upside if correct)

WEB RESEARCH FINDINGS:
{search_findings}

SMART MONEY / TRADER POSITIONING DATA:
{smart_money_context}

Based on all the above data, produce a comprehensive trading opportunity assessment.

You MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON object using this exact schema:
{{
  "ai_score": <integer 0-100, overall opportunity quality>,
  "risk_level": "low" | "medium" | "high",
  "pnl_potential": <float 0-1, potential profit if correct>,
  "credibility_score": <integer 0-100, how credible/researchable is this market>,
  "smart_money_signal": "bullish" | "bearish" | "neutral",
  "smart_money_summary": "Brief description of what smart money/whales are doing",
  "recommendation": "strong_buy" | "buy" | "hold" | "avoid",
  "recommended_side": "YES" | "NO",
  "reasoning": "2-3 sentence explanation of the scoring and recommendation",
  "search_summary": "Brief summary of key findings from web research",
  "key_risks": ["risk1", "risk2", "risk3"]
}}

opportunity_analysis.event_scoring:
Analyze this Polymarket EVENT GROUP (multiple related sub-markets under one event) and identify the best trading opportunity:

EVENT: {event_title}

SUB-MARKET OPTIONS:
{sub_markets_table}

Aggregate Event Volume: ${event_volume}
Aggregate Event Liquidity: ${event_liquidity}

WEB RESEARCH FINDINGS:
{search_findings}

SMART MONEY / TRADER POSITIONING DATA:
{smart_money_context}

You are analyzing all sub-markets in this event as a group. Identify which specific option represents the best risk/reward opportunity and explain why.

You MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON object using this exact schema:
{{
  "ai_score": <integer 0-100, overall event opportunity quality>,
  "risk_level": "low" | "medium" | "high",
  "pnl_potential": <float 0-1, potential profit on best option>,
  "credibility_score": <integer 0-100, how credible/researchable is this event>,
  "smart_money_signal": "bullish" | "bearish" | "neutral",
  "smart_money_summary": "Brief description of what smart money/whales are doing across event",
  "recommendation": "strong_buy" | "buy" | "hold" | "avoid",
  "recommended_side": "YES" | "NO",
  "recommended_option": "<exact groupItemTitle of the best sub-market to trade>",
  "reasoning": "2-3 sentence explanation covering the full event context and why this option is best",
  "search_summary": "Brief summary of key findings from web research",
  "key_risks": ["risk1", "risk2", "risk3"]
}}

opportunity_analysis.event_quick_analysis:
Provide a QUICK grouped-trade analysis for this Polymarket event with multiple options.

EVENT: {event_title}
EVENT SLUG: {event_slug}

SUB-MARKET OPTIONS:
{sub_markets_table}

Aggregate Event Volume: ${event_volume}
Aggregate Event Liquidity: ${event_liquidity}

Treat this event as ONE trade decision with multiple choices. Identify the best option and side based on pricing and structure only (no web research). Keep the summary concise.

You MUST respond with ONLY valid JSON using this exact schema:
{{
  "analysis": "2-3 sentence grouped quick analysis",
  "recommended_option": "<best option label exactly as listed in table>",
  "recommended_side": "YES" | "NO"
}}

copy_trading.trade_evaluation:
